T*
(This paper studies model merging for efficient reuse of language models.) Tj
T*
(Model merging combines parameters from independently trained expert models.) Tj
T*
(Parameter interpolation is a simple baseline that averages model weights.) Tj
T*
(Task arithmetic can add or subtract learned parameter update vectors.) Tj
T*
(The evaluation compares merged models on accuracy and robustness benchmarks.) Tj
T*
(Good merge coefficients preserve useful capabilities from every source model.) Tj
T*
(Our retrieval prototype extracts text from PDF documents before chunking.) Tj
T*
(Each chunk receives a deterministic local hashing embedding for development.) Tj
T*
(The backend computes cosine similarity between a query and indexed chunks.) Tj
T*
(Results are sorted by similarity score and the top ranked chunks are returned.) Tj
T*
(The web application sends requests to the backend REST API over HTTP.) Tj
T*
(A future Slack bot will call the same API and will contain no search logic.) Tj
T*
(The repository abstraction can later use Supabase and pgvector search.) Tj
T*
(The embedding provider can later be replaced by Gemini or an E5 model.) Tj
T*
(This Phase One system intentionally omits answer generation and reranking.) Tj
